# A compiled factory whose generated body fails to compile is rejected at the
# use site, with the failing compiler diagnostic and a note pointing at the
# factory definition with file:line.  This .ccs factory has no #line directive,
# so the note falls back to the use-site input file and the buffer line where
# `bad_slot_factory` is defined (line 8).  The _Generic mismatch wording
# is the host compiler's and varies (gcc/clang/tcc), so it is not pinned.
comptime_emit_bad_slot_fail.ccs:23:5: error: type: compiled generic factory 'BadSlot' failed to compile
note: in @comptime factory 'bad_slot_factory' at
comptime_emit_bad_slot_fail.ccs:8
